# Lesson plan curriculum bundle: force LF line endings so the bundled
# copies stay byte-identical to the upstream limitless-academy/ source
# after any checkout — including Windows checkouts where the user has
# `core.autocrlf=true` set globally. Without this, every Windows
# checkout converts the .md files to CRLF and the sync script
# (scripts/sync-lesson-plans.{sh,ps1}) reports them as drifted on
# every run, even when the upstream LF copies are unchanged.
src-tauri/lesson_plans/**/*.md text eol=lf

# Sync script uses bash conventions; force LF so it's executable on
# any platform that picks up its own line endings from autocrlf.
scripts/sync-lesson-plans.sh text eol=lf
